# Git push (Dastak)

When the user says **push**, **deploy**, **ship it**, or similar, **commit any pending project changes and push to the remote immediately**. Do not ask "Want this pushed?" or wait for a second confirmation.

- Follow the existing git safety protocol (status, diff, commit message, `git pull --rebase` if needed, then push).
- Use smart-mode approval for protected `main` when the environment requires it; do not ask the user in chat first.
- After finishing a task the user clearly wanted on the live repo, you may push once if they already said push in that thread; otherwise only push when they explicitly request it (do not auto-commit unrelated WIP without a push/deploy request).

At the end of responses, **do not** offer "Say if you want this pushed" — the user will say push when they want it.
